## Neighbouring structures already worth learning from

Current bTB exploration alone has surfaced useful owners:
- One Health — integrated human/animal/ecosystem health;
- adaptive management — decision-linked monitoring and learning under uncertainty;
- participatory epidemiology — local/community knowledge as epidemiological intelligence, triangulated with conventional methods;
- policy feedback — policies reshape later capacities, beliefs, participation and politics;
- just-transition work — phase-out is inseparable from replacement capacity, affected communities and sequencing.

These are examples, not a closed reading list. Better external structure should be learned, credited and connected.

## Use rule

This issue is not a demand to expand TRACE.

For any item:

```text
EXPLORE FREELY
-> LEARN FROM OWNERS
-> CONNECT ACROSS DOMAINS
-> FIND CONSEQUENCE
-> ONLY THEN ASK WHETHER DURABLE MACHINERY CHANGES
```

An item may remain permanently as understanding without becoming schema, canon or even a named project concept.

## Anti-closure rule

Do not mark this horizon "complete".

When exploration reveals another major territory, add it or link it. When two territories turn out to be the same underlying object, connect them rather than deleting the history that exposed the connection.

The desired failure mode is **too much discoverable horizon with selective cognition**, not a falsely complete small map.

`HORIZON_COMPLETENESS = DISCOVERABILITY, NOT COMPULSORY_COGNITION`.
